6
00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:21.260
The semiconductor industry is staring at a
physical wall.

7
00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:24.060
For decades, Moore's Law — the observation
that transistor

8
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:26.220
counts double roughly every two years —
has held

9
00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:28.500
true. But as transistors shrink to just a
few

10
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:30.460
nanometers wide, the rules of physics
change.

11
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:32.160
Electrons leak. Heat builds up.

12
00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:33.980
Manufacturing becomes brutally difficult.

13
00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:37.060
Silicon, the foundation of the modern
world, is approaching

14
00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:38.520
